      "id": 1,
      "text": "Glyfada's name comes from salt‑water wells that were abundant in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glyfada",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Glyfada stretches from the foot of Hymettus to the Saronic Gulf, giving it both mountain and sea views.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glyfada",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The suburb grew from an unassuming coastal town into a lively Athens Riviera hotspot after a tram line linked it to Syntagma and Piraeus for the 2004 Olympics.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.thisisathens.org/neighbourhoods/glyfada-guide",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Glyfada Marina spans 3 km of waterfront, with basins A through G forming a continuous harbor for yachts and leisure boats.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glyfada",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town hosts some of Athens' best‑known nightclubs, upscale restaurants, and shops, making it a nightlife hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glyfada",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
